{"type":"message","id":"d1c83e6b","parentId":"5f1b5c29","timestamp":"2026-06-03T14:33:42.237Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The total is still 773 for both threads. The messages I sent didn't increase the total count. This suggests that the messages might not have been properly stored, or they were stored but with the same ID (overwriting), or the endpoint is returning 200 but not actually storing the messages.\n\nWait, actually looking at the total - before it was 773, and it's still 773. Let me look at this differently. The issue might be that the GET /send endpoint returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" regardless, and it might not actually be storing messages.\n\nBut wait - maybe the messages are stored with a delay? Or maybe they ARE stored but the history is returning the same count because of pagination issues?\n \nI'm realizing the GET /send endpoint might just be a status check that always returns 200, not actually storing anything. Let me try switching to the POST method instead, but I'm running into issues with JSON formatting in the URL-encoded query string. When I tried POST earlier, I got a 500 error with error code 1101, so the JSON body might be getting corrupted in the request.\n\nActually, I'm noticing the root endpoint returns 401 Unauthorized, but the /history endpoint with the API key works fine while /send returns 500. This could be a Cloudflare Workers error code 1101 — maybe the runtime is hitting a limit or the endpoint doesn't support POST at all. Let me look up what error 1101 actually means in Cloudflare's context to figure out if there's a different endpoint I should be using or if this is a configuration issue on their end.","thinkingSignature":"c42a6717e35c75e9465d19d013889535578ec8f1c8fba65ff28c8535fbb1d990"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qldk3mhipfxi_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try POST with proper JSON escaping\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.